# Convergence — F0 quality proposal refinement

AC-01..04: APPROVED for documentary preparation only, after reexamination of the
expanded contract. Current review: docs/validation/f0-reconciliation-20261101/quality-refinement/review.md.
The predecessor envelope/convergence and six other files are preserved byte-for-byte
in quality-refinement/before/; earlier observations remain historical and unchanged.

T010/T011 refine Q01–Q13, map them to all seven F0 rows and revise D1–D4 plus a
separate proposed F0-D5 version-update ADR. Coverage distinguishes total/changed
executable lines; regressions require defective/corrected cases; performance needs
baseline then adopted budgets. UI, security, effective cancellation and extension
contracts have observable expectations.

Comparison checked 120 prior bindings: six intended document inputs changed.
Eight predecessors and 85 protected product/storage/authority inputs retain their
hashes; 36 skill scenarios match recorded contracts/statuses. Correct global
structure passed; freshness rejected the old envelope for six stale inputs and
the new AC-04 binding. Eight existing evidence tests passed. Final freshness,
links/policy and whitespace results are in quality-refinement/checks-final.json.
Initial wrongly scoped validator calls checked no feature; initial-checks.json
preserves them and excludes their exit zero from feature acceptance.

F0 remains open: four INCONCLUSIVE and three UNVERIFIED rows. Expanded Q01–Q13
are operationally UNVERIFIED. T006 remains the maintainer's F0-D1–D5 adoption
record. No dependency upgrade, coverage/performance measurement, Cargo/GUI replay,
threat-control implementation, storage experiment or product reacceptance occurred.
Rust 1.99.1, Iced =0.14.0, Cargo.lock and project authorities remain unchanged.

Resume with adoption/amendment, then G2's clause-level inventory: implemented with
sufficient evidence, implemented without sufficient evidence, absent or justified
outside scope. Methods/budgets and bounded tests/fixes follow actual gaps.
Persistence AC-01..07 remain UNVERIFIED; independent pre-MVP storage needs its
separate decisions. Current volatile-history honesty remains applicable even if
storage implementation is deferred.

